Z||000003||Kelvin Vivian||07-16-2001||02:52 AM||||Seanh,<P>I thought that the seats may have been recovered, but I'm pretty sure it's not the case... The driver side seat had it's headrest ripped apart because someone was looking for headrest speakers, but none were there, luckily they didn't tear up the passenger side seat... I'll post pics of the seat soon.<P>Toddster,<BR>It was chilly  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, I had to had to bail around 12:30p, had to get back to studying. I had a good time, it was nice seeing a bunch of Fieros all together.<P>Cars that I thought were neat, in no particular order:<P>- A Black 88 GT T-top, with the driver-side visor autographed by Hulki Aldikacti.<BR>- A BRIGHT Red 88 GT T-Top with 21,000 miles, had the original p-seals in good condition. <BR>- Chris West's 3.8? dual overhead cam Red Fiero.<BR>- A stock white 88 Mera, first Mera I ever saw in person.<BR>- I also liked the two 85 2M6s that were there. I don't see too many of those on the road.<P>I wonder who won the raffle car? It was an 86 SE V6, 4-spd, sunroof, spoiler.<P>Give me a call when you next work on your GT, I'll help you finish her up. Then I need to take a look at how my exhaust pipes are running, I had a muffler shop cut out a kink and reweld in a new section (4-cyl Duke runs A LOT smoother and stronger now), I think I just need to pry the exhaust pipe away from the frame...<P>Good stuff... If anyone has seats with speaker holes with no speakers inside, I'd like to hear from you... ||||reg||1
